  "prefLabel": "He-M 1201.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2020-03-23",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-M 1201.01 Purpose. The purpose of these rules is to establish minimum standards for individuals’ health coordination and to ensure the safe administration of medications by providers to individuals who receive services pursuant to He-M 1001, He-M 507, He-M 518, He-M 521, He-M 524, or He-M 525 as applicable.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at part heading for He-M 1201) #4809, eff 5-1-90; amd by #5246, eff 10-8-91; ss by #6000, eff 3-21-95; ss by #7836, INTERIM, eff 3-22-03, EXPIRES: 9-18-03; ss by #7956, eff 9-19-03; ss by #9982, eff 9-19-11; ss by #12876, INTERIM, eff 9-25-19, EXPIRES: 3-23-20; ss by #13009, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 3-23-20; ss by #13057, eff 6-17-20",
